  "caption": "When Uncle Ray was told he had Parkinson's, his plan was simple: we move, together. Quinn signed up as training buddy and was promptly out-walked on day one.\n\nStructured exercise can help movement and quality of life with Parkinson's, and the benefits tend to fade if you stop — so it works best as a lifelong habit, started early.\n\nWhat can help: big-amplitude movement, external cues like counting or a line to step over at doorways, supervised walk-and-talk practice, leg strength and balance work, and dance or water classes you enjoy.\n\nSee your GP or neurologist for sudden worsening, a fall with a head knock, new confusion, fainting on standing or a rapid loss of walking.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
